+# BLUE CURRENT V51.45.0 — MANAGEMENT & EXECUTIVE ACCURACY
+
+V51.41–V51.45 hardens management and executive reporting so pilot-critical KPIs cannot look trustworthy merely because a dashboard can display a plausible number.
+
+## Major issue found and corrected
+
+The Executive Command Center still contained deterministic/modelled fallback values for several locations when authoritative restaurant data was missing.
+
+Those fallbacks could create plausible-looking values for:
+
+- revenue
+- prior-day revenue/trend
+- table counts / occupancy
+- guest counts
+- ticket counts/timing
+- staff counts
+- health
+
+V51.45 removes those deterministic KPI fallbacks from the executive surface.
+
+Missing authoritative metrics now remain:
+
+`null / unavailable`
+
+instead of being silently modeled.
+
+The Executive UI was also hardened so unavailable metrics display as:
+
+`—`
+
+rather than being converted to zero.
+
+## Executive data policy
+
+The Executive Command Center now reports:
+
+- `syntheticFallbacks: false`
+- `missingAuthoritativeMetricsRemainNull: true`
+- `financialMetricsRequireFinancialSource: true`
+
+Every location includes provenance metadata and:
+
+- `syntheticFallbackUsed: false`
+
+## Accuracy certification layer
+
+V51.45 adds source reconciliation for:
+
+- occupancy
+- active reservations
+- active waitlist
+- active staff
+- active kitchen tickets
+- guest / cover count
+- revenue
+
+The certification compares the Executive Command Center value against authoritative source collections.
+
+Possible states:
+
+- MATCH
+- DISCREPANCY
+- UNVERIFIED
+- MISSING_DISPLAY_VALUE
+
+## Authoritative sources
+
+Current operational sources include:
+
+- tables
+- reservations
+- waitlist
+- staff
+- kitchenTickets
+
+Revenue requires an actual financial source, such as:
+
+- financialSnapshots
+- locationFinancials
+- revenueSnapshots
+
+A deterministic or modeled revenue number can never satisfy revenue provenance.
+
+## Portfolio reconciliation
+
+Portfolio occupancy, guest count, and revenue are also reconciled against location source data.
+
+Critical location/portfolio discrepancies or unverified revenue block certification.
+
+## Current authenticated Chefs runtime after hardening
+
+Status:
+
+`management-executive-accuracy-blocked`
+
+Current location metric comparisons:
+
+- 35 total
+- 22 MATCH
+- 0 DISCREPANCY
+- 13 UNVERIFIED
+- 10 critical trust issues
+
+The important change is that after synthetic fallback removal there are now:
+
+`0 discrepancies caused by fabricated fallback values`
+
+Missing metrics are explicitly UNVERIFIED instead.
+
+Current executive portfolio:
+
+- occupancy: 15%
+- guest count: 2
+- revenue: unavailable
+- data complete: false
+
+Location revenue is currently unavailable for all five restaurants because no authoritative financial source exists in the current dataset.
+
+Marina Grille:
+
+- occupancy: source-backed
+- revenue: unavailable
+
+Harbor House / River & Rail / The Cabin / Garden Social:
+
+- occupancy: unavailable because floor data is not populated
+- revenue: unavailable because financial data is not connected
+
+That is the correct pilot-safe behavior.
+
+## Human certification
+
+Adds:
+
+GET `/api/management-executive-accuracy`
+
+POST `/api/management-executive-accuracy/certify`
+
+Final certification requires:
+
+- zero critical executive-data trust issues
+- authoritative financial provenance for revenue
+- human executive-accuracy evidence
+- human certification note
+- admin permission
+
+Certified state:
+
+`MANAGEMENT_EXECUTIVE_ACCURACY_CERTIFIED`
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- source tracing required
+- critical discrepancies block trust
+- unverified revenue blocks certification
+- stale/missing source stays visible
+- human certification required
+- no synthetic executive pass
+- no automatic metric correction
+- no automatic financial inference
+- autonomous production changes false
+
